<title>RUSSIA: Russia to offer 11.5 trln rbls in bills Feb 12.</title>
<headline>Russia to offer 11.5 trln rbls in bills Feb 12.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Russian Finance Ministry will offer 4.5 trillion roubles in 196-day GKO discount Treasury bills (series 22071) and seven trillion roubles in 287-day T-bills (series 22072) on February 12, the central bank said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Full details of the auctions follow:  </p>
<p>Full details of 196-day auction:</p>
<p>    Series number		  22071</p>
<p>    Issue volume		   4.50 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations		  1.00 million</p>
<p>    Issue date		     Feb 12, 1997</p>
<p>    Tenor			    196 days</p>
<p>    Maturity			 Aug 27, 1997</p>
<p>Full details of 287-day auction:</p>
<p>    Series number		  22072</p>
<p>    Issue volume		   7.00 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations		  1.00 million</p>
<p>    Issue date		     Feb 12, 1997</p>
<p>    Tenor			    287 days</p>
<p>    Maturity			 Nov 26, 1997</p>
<p>On February 12 the Finance Ministry will repay about 7.68 trillion roubles in maturing six-month T-bill (series 22042).</p>
<p>--Julie Tolkacheva, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
